## What the reviewer got wrong (not applied as requested)

- Space as the Lithuanian thousands separator is the right typographic habit, and the Minguo-to-Gregorian equivalents (109 = 2020, 112 = 2023) are right. Both were not applied because the checker cannot parse a space group or an added Gregorian digit (R14, R13, ACCEPTED-ROUND).
- Reformatting „TWD 1.57M“ to „1,57 mln. TWD“ is right as Lithuanian, and wrong for this pack: the test pins those bytes.
- Deleting U+200B and promoting Q16–Q20 to headings would read better. The Korean source has the same zero-width spaces and the same heading levels, and the checker compares those counts. The lines stay.
- On 018, „platintojas“ is wrong for the title and the contracts row (English: agent). It is not wrong for the FAQ „start through a distributor“ or for the early-export distribution contract. Those two stay.
- The 004 link really is the withholding-rate standard, article 3 (`flno=3`), not Business Tax Act article 10. The Korean/English link text still says article 10, and the checker counts that 10. The label now names article 3 and still contains 10 so the number bag matches. A label with only „3 straipsnis“ fails numbers.
